president  party secretary the people's leader and  to some  just papa she xi jinping is called many  things and as the communist party  celebrates its 100 year anniversary  the 68 year old is consolidating his  position as the country's most  powerful leader in decades the party has  united and it led the people  in opening a great path making great  achievements  forging a great spirit she has led china  for nine years  and after abolishing presidential term  limits in 2018  is unlikely to step down anytime soon he  began his term with an anti-corruption  campaign  which saw one and a half million  officials punished it also  purged the party of any opposition to  his rule  she then promised to end extreme poverty  nationwide  a promise he said he fulfilled last year  many say  these feats have given rise to a status  on par with the party founder mao zedong  the chinese people have advanced very  well and they don't want to give that up  and they won't and they they'll they'll  attach themselves to any leader  who is able to you know not only promise  but deliver  the son of revolutionary elites she was  sent to rural northeastern china during  the cultural revolution  where he joined the party and rose  through the ranks  china has since transformed into the  second largest economy in the world  with technological prowess second only  to the us  and growing global influence his  admirers say she is the ideal person  to bring china into the modern era  critics say  he is a dictator so that's like a  natural curse  for any dictatorship however it may be  mighty  maybe effective maybe charismatic at the  beginning  over time a dictatorship will decay  simply because  you know it does not have the kind of a  diversity  kind of sensible debate over policies  under his watch  authorities have cracked down on descent  in hong kong and xinyong  and according to human rights groups  imprisoned up to one million uighurs in  re-education camps  for she the battle to maintain power  isn't just political  it's ideological for now in china  only one path leads to the greatest  rewards  the path of loyalty to the leader  so certainly there was a really great  extravagant spectacle held this morning  on thursday here in beijing in tiananmen  square 70 000 people gathering  uh with precision like performance  really sending this official message  to not only the chinese people but to  the world so there's two ways to read  this one is to take it at face value  that  the party has made china stronger than  ever before  and that it will continue to succeed and  it's proven  that this system which it refers to as  socialism with chinese characteristics  has worked for china and it will work  for the rest of the world another way to  read this  is that this is just the surface and  potentially underneath  really the communist party is extremely  insecure that  it is extremely insecure that at any  point it could lose grip on  an increasingly educated creative  and informed group of 1.4 billion  people and it needs huge ideological  propaganda events like this  in order to help retain their loyalty  which it could lose  at any time

